  "content_en": "Sister Wen Shi stood at the door. She was wearing a new cloak with bright red peonies and a faint light on her face, which made her lips red and white, her teeth bright and beautiful. Although she is only eleven or twelve years old and her eyebrows have not yet grown, she is already a pretty girl. \"Cold? You know it's cold, but others don't. Could it be that everyone else is made of steel, but you are made of flesh and blood?\" Ms. Jiang looked at her daughter's outstanding face, and the innocent look on her face that was ignorant of the world. She couldn't help but feel a little less angry, but she still scolded her with a straight face. Born into such a complex and huge family, beauty alone is not enough. The most important thing is to be transparent, stable and humane. \"Mom, don't blame me.\" Seeing Mrs. Jiang's displeasure, Sister Wen Shi hurried over and hugged Mr. Jiang's arm like a baby. \"My daughter realized her mistake. She woke up at first, but somehow she fell asleep again. It was too late when she opened her eyes again. \"Stop shaking, it's making me panic. Go and sit down with your ninth sister for a while while I put on my coat, and we'll go to the main room to pay my respects to the old lady!\" Mrs. Jiang couldn't bear to say harsh words. Cuimei Cuiqiao helped Mrs. Jiang to get dressed in the inner room, while the tenth sister walked to the ninth sister's side to greet her, and then sat down next to her. \"Sister Ninth is so early every day, I'm really ashamed of my sister.\" A little maid had already brought a teacup, and Sister Wen was blowing the tea gently while chatting with Sister Ninth. \"Is this...\" Sister Ninth smiled, \"Don't be embarrassed, sister. I have always been a light sleeper. I asked the doctor to see it the first year, and the doctor said it was innate.\" \"Oh, is that so?\" Sister Wen was a little surprised, but she still nodded. Sister Jiu smiled again. She doesn't hate this sister-in-law, maybe it's because she was cared for so well by the Jiang family. She is a very simple child who is easy to fool around with, so the two of them get along well. Of course, most of this is due to her generosity and humility. Otherwise, let alone saying that this is her sister-in-law, just say that with her two lifetimes combined, she is several dozen years old. Let her compete with a teenage child, which is not boring at all. \"Sister Ninth's hand stove is so exquisite. Did you ask someone to take it out?\" Sister Wen's eyes suddenly fell on her hand, and her face was slightly restrained. Sister Jiu glanced at her and said, \"Of course not, it was because my mother looked coldly at me just now!\" After saying that, his eyes dropped and lingered on the red peony cloak she was wearing for a moment before turning to her face again. Sister Wen Shi was slightly startled, and quickly lowered her head to take a sip of tea to cover up the discomfort on her face. She was really stingy. She wanted a new cloak made of good quality material, so her mother asked someone to make it for her. This sister didn't even hum. Now that she saw such a small hand stove, she really shouldn't have. \"Sister, do you know how to read the book Mr. Yun asked you to memorize yesterday?\" With one look, he calmed down the resentment and turned passivity into initiative. It was a huge move, but Sister Wenjiu did not dare to be careless because she only felt that there was a sharp edge behind her. \"Of course I know how to do it. I learned it by heart last night.\" Upon hearing this, Sister Ten's face immediately showed a little smile and she said with a smile. She is not only a little beauty, but also a little talented girl. Although she is a little confused at embroidery, she is good at literacy and endorsement. \"Ninth sister, what about you?\" Tenth sister asked again. \"I...\" Sister Wen Jiu was startled, and then lowered her head in confusion, \"I don't know how to do it yet, but... there's just one more thing...\" \"One more thing? Oh... Sister Ninth, you're not doing this right, you should have worked on it earlier, but it's okay, I'll teach you to save you from being punished by your master for a while.\" Sister Wen Shi not only did not laugh at her, but said enthusiastically. This is the key to Sister Ninth's not resenting this little girl. Although she is occasionally a little petty, she has a good heart. \"Okay, thank you so much, sister.\" Sister Jiu smiled and thanked her. Sister Wen Shi began to recite in a low voice, and asked Sister Ninth to repeat one sentence after reciting it. Looking at the little girl's serious look, Sister Jiu couldn't help but want to laugh in her heart. How could she not? In her previous life, in order to get into the ideal university, she had to overcome all obstacles and squeeze into the single-plank bridge, study hard, and work hard, but unfortunately, alas... As Sister Wen muttered in a low voice, Sister Ninth pretended to be unintentional and turned sideways. Out of the corner of her eye, she caught sight of Mother Zhou turning away, and her heart suddenly relaxed. Sometimes it is not easy to hide one's clumsiness. It can be hidden from these little girls, but it is not easy to hide it from those old men. After what happened yesterday, she didn't dare to be careless again, otherwise her aunt, who was dignified and generous on the surface but was actually suspicious, would think of her... In a short time, the Jiang family had already come out, and thatSister Ninth and Sister Ten went out together. \"Mother, didn't you say a few days ago that you saw a chinchilla leather material for making a cloak? Why... haven't you made it yet?\" But the tenth sister did not move, her eyes fell on Jiang's old gray crane-colored brocade silk cloak. \"Do you have to do it after seeing it?\" After hearing her words, Mrs. Jiang couldn't help but frown and glance at her. Sister Wen Shi was startled. Jiang ignored her and headed out the door. Looking at her mother's back, Sister Wenshi couldn't help but shed tears in her beautiful eyes. Mother Zhou followed Mrs. Jiang, glanced at Sister Wen Shi, hesitated to speak, then shook her head, turned around and followed Mr. Jiang. \"Ninth sister...\" At that moment, only the ninth sister was left in the room, and the tenth sister immediately called her, her tone full of grievances. \"Let's go, sister, mother may be anxious!\" Sister Jiu immediately stepped forward, took her arm, and went out. In fact, Sister Ninth was quite puzzled by this scene. When her beloved daughter asked about the cloak, she was met with such an attitude. Of course she wouldn't think it was because of the old one she was wearing. Wasn't the cloak Jiang was wearing last year? It seems that what my aunt said yesterday is true. The Jiang family's business is indeed in trouble. The Jiang family has really begun to hold on to their dowry and even considered selling off the subsidies. I wonder if the advanced technology she donated yesterday can help? Of course she hopes to help. Can a boat be lifted when the water rises? Going out from the corner door in the courtyard is the garden, and through the garden is the main hall of the entire Hou Mansion. The Hou Mansion is divided into five parts. The east side houses the big and third rooms, the west side houses the second and fourth rooms, and the Yanshou Hall of the old lady Li is in the center. \"Haha, dear baby, come quickly...come, let my great-grandmother take a good look...\" It was obvious that Jiang and his party arrived late. Before they even approached the Yanshou Hall, a burst of laughter came from inside. It can be seen that it is very lively inside. Jiang paused, his face full of solemnity, as if he was facing a formidable enemy...",
